From 52ea534cdfce7258a0a4ef3d73ada3e1653b23c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:17:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci(linux): build the Linux AppImage in a reproducible
 container

Add docker/Dockerfile and docker/Makefile defining the Linux build
environment (the linux-build-deps/apt.txt packages plus SDL2/SDL2_net/tinyxml2/
libzip built from source, frozen into image layers) and rewire the Linux job of
generate-builds.yml to produce its AppImage with `make -C docker appimage`.

The container mirrors the job's ubuntu-22.04 / gcc-12 environment exactly,
folding in the install-sdl2-net and install-tinyxml2 composite-action steps; it
is arch-generic so both legs of the x86_64/aarch64 build matrix are preserved.
The only intended change is freezing those from-source library steps into image
layers, so the build is reproducible and a developer can run the identical build
locally. The generate-soh-otr job and the uploaded artifacts are unchanged: each
matrix leg still downloads soh.o2r into build-cmake/soh, where the build bundles
it.

The .gitignore gains `!docker/Makefile`: the repo's blanket CMake `Makefile`
ignore would otherwise hide the new committed file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
